#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186269157 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "14223e47-647d-5b4d-a877-694192638d49" :knowledge-point/title "Expressing a Position Vector in Component Form Given Its Graph"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "6a9735d0-1428-56cd-b110-f96c0bdccf2a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186269159}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "6a9735d0-1428-56cd-b110-f96c0bdccf2a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186269159} :answer-field/id #uuid "f20dff8a-4f1a-5d3f-8e76-ac7f060f5cea" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186269158} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "d980e5fa-559b-5c15-8a3d-e2fbca685352" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186269161}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d980e5fa-559b-5c15-8a3d-e2fbca685352" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186269161} :answer-field/id #uuid "f830c1de-5be2-58b3-966d-726aafec77a2" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186269160} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b48c3a91-45b4-528a-a10f-0875e4c8e377" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186269163}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b48c3a91-45b4-528a-a10f-0875e4c8e377" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186269163} :answer-field/id #uuid "7adc6ce3-cd05-514f-ad76-93449c7b43f2" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186269162}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "9c809f02-6e43-5132-a6eb-86592919e2e2" :question/math-academy-id "q-168031" :question/problem "An ambulance service helicopter takes off from a hospital helipad three times on a particular day. The helicopter's location a few seconds after these takeoffs are given by points $P,$ $Q,$ and $R.$\n\nCurrent part:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13964559/assets/e589960ec2647179ac013cf60286129ece1d31e5daa8bf16fdeb237e942c92df.png)     \n                                \n                            \n\n   \n\n                            The helicopter's pilot represents the three locations in vector form, as shown in the diagram. Taking the helipad as the origin, find the coordinates of the position vectors $p,$ $q,$ and $r$ of the points $P,$ $Q,$ and $R,$ respectively.\n\n                            \n                                    \n                                        \n                                            \n\n                                                \n\n                                        \n                                        \n                                        \n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        $p=⟨$\n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                            \n                                        {{field-1}}                \n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        \n$,\\,0,\\,3⟩\\,,$ \n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                                \n\n                                                \n\n                                        \n                                        \n                                        \n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        $q=⟨0,\\,-3,\\,$\n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                            \n                                        {{field-2}}                \n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        \n$⟩\\,,$ \n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                                \n\n                                                \n\n                                        \n                                        \n                                        \n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        $r=⟨0,\\,$ \n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                            \n                                        {{field-3}}                \n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        \n$,\\,3⟩\\,.$" :question/worked-solution "Remember that in general, if a point $A$ has coordinates $({a}_{x},{a}_{y},{a}_{z}),$ then its position vector is given by\n\n$$\n\\overset{\\to }{OA}=⟨{a}_{x},{a}_{y},{a}_{z}⟩.\n$$\n\nHere, the point $P$ has coordinates $(0,0,3),$ so its position vector is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}p & =⟨0,0,3⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe point $Q$ has coordinates $(0,-3,2),$ so its position vector is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}q & =⟨0,-3,2⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe point $R$ has coordinates $(0,4,3),$ so its position vector is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r & =⟨0,4,3⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186269164 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "33f0ec6b-9cb4-5246-9ac6-23b35e3b224e" :knowledge-point/title "Expressing a Vector as a Sum or Difference of More Than Two Known Vectors"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "76731614-c56c-5245-b0cc-ee103b4b8646" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "r-q" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186269166}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "76731614-c56c-5245-b0cc-ee103b4b8646" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "r-q" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186269166} :answer-field/id #uuid "44739811-9cfd-5dd3-8d4e-9b062347608d" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186269165}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "9248a24e-4292-5cb5-b331-1a414ca368e7" :question/math-academy-id "q-168032" :question/problem "An ambulance service helicopter takes off from a hospital helipad three times on a particular day. The helicopter's location a few seconds after these takeoffs are given by points $P,$ $Q,$ and $R.$\n\nEarlier part 1:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13964559/assets/e589960ec2647179ac013cf60286129ece1d31e5daa8bf16fdeb237e942c92df.png)     \n                                \n                            \n\n   \n\n                            The helicopter's pilot represents the three locations in vector form, as shown in the diagram. Taking the helipad as the origin, find the coordinates of the position vectors $p,$ $q,$ and $r$ of the points $P,$ $Q,$ and $R,$ respectively.\n\n                            \n                                    \n                                        \n                                            \n\n                                                \n\n                                        \n                                        \n                                        \n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        $p=⟨$\n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                            \n                                        $0$                \n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        \n$,\\,0,\\,3⟩\\,,$ \n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                                \n\n                                                \n\n                                        \n                                        \n                                        \n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        $q=⟨0,\\,-3,\\,$\n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                            \n                                        $2$                \n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        \n$⟩\\,,$ \n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                                \n\n                                                \n\n                                        \n                                        \n                                        \n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        $r=⟨0,\\,$ \n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                            \n                                        $4$                \n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        \n$,\\,3⟩\\,.$\n\nCurrent part:\n\nExpress the vector $x=\\overset{\\to }{QR}$ in terms of the vectors $q$ and $r.$\n\n                            \n                                    \n                                        \n                                            \n\n                                                \n\n                                        \n                                        \n                                        \n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        $x\\,=\\,$\n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                            \n                                        {{field-1}}                \n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                         $\\text{ }$ (Type the vectors $q$ and $r$ as $q$ and $r$, respectively)." :question/worked-solution "According to the triangle law of addition, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{QR} & =\\overset{\\to }{OR}-\\overset{\\to }{OQ} \\\\ x & =r-q.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186269167 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "8f819127-1ab3-5a85-a381-9e30e32884aa" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating Sums and Differences of Vectors"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "da49ca74-3f86-5e7d-87c4-98f7ad65c42c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186269169}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "da49ca74-3f86-5e7d-87c4-98f7ad65c42c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186269169} :answer-field/id #uuid "de779902-6fb8-5499-a0c0-6f14c56115f6" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186269168} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "47c22e0a-8962-596d-a2ce-b7f449d5278f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "7" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186269171}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "47c22e0a-8962-596d-a2ce-b7f449d5278f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "7" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186269171} :answer-field/id #uuid "7f3d38b1-e094-5063-83ff-1c65378f92e2" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186269170} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b904102f-71fc-5d95-952c-c483e046285d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186269173}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b904102f-71fc-5d95-952c-c483e046285d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186269173} :answer-field/id #uuid "131412c6-86ee-5b16-bbfb-fff028600141" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186269172}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "1c4c0f9d-dbfc-5a9d-8c30-31acfce1c91d" :question/math-academy-id "q-168033" :question/problem "An ambulance service helicopter takes off from a hospital helipad three times on a particular day. The helicopter's location a few seconds after these takeoffs are given by points $P,$ $Q,$ and $R.$\n\nEarlier part 1:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13964559/assets/e589960ec2647179ac013cf60286129ece1d31e5daa8bf16fdeb237e942c92df.png)     \n                                \n                            \n\n   \n\n                            The helicopter's pilot represents the three locations in vector form, as shown in the diagram. Taking the helipad as the origin, find the coordinates of the position vectors $p,$ $q,$ and $r$ of the points $P,$ $Q,$ and $R,$ respectively.\n\n                            \n                                    \n                                        \n                                            \n\n                                                \n\n                                        \n                                        \n                                        \n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        $p=⟨$\n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                            \n                                        $0$                \n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        \n$,\\,0,\\,3⟩\\,,$ \n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                                \n\n                                                \n\n                                        \n                                        \n                                        \n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        $q=⟨0,\\,-3,\\,$\n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                            \n                                        $2$                \n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        \n$⟩\\,,$ \n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                                \n\n                                                \n\n                                        \n                                        \n                                        \n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        $r=⟨0,\\,$ \n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                            \n                                        $4$                \n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        \n$,\\,3⟩\\,.$\n\nEarlier part 2:\n\nExpress the vector $x=\\overset{\\to }{QR}$ in terms of the vectors $q$ and $r.$\n\n                            \n                                    \n                                        \n                                            \n\n                                                \n\n                                        \n                                        \n                                        \n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        $x\\,=\\,$\n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                            \n                                        $r-q$                \n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                         $\\text{ }$ (Type the vectors $q$ and $r$ as $q$ and $r$, respectively).\n\nCurrent part:\n\nFind the components of vector $x.$\n\n                            \n                                    \n                                        \n                                            \n\n                                                \n\n                                        \n                                        \n                                        \n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        $x=⟨$\n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                            \n                                        {{field-1}}                \n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        \n$,\\,$\n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                            \n                                        {{field-2}}                \n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        \n$,\\,$\n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                            \n                                        {{field-3}}                \n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        \n$⟩$" :question/worked-solution "From part 1, we have $q=⟨0,-3,2⟩$ and $r=⟨0,4,3⟩.$\n\nAlso, from part 2, we have $x=r-q$\n\nTo compute the difference of two vectors, we just subtract each component individually:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r-q & =⟨0,4,3⟩-⟨0,-3,2⟩ \\\\  & =⟨0-0,4-(-3),3-2⟩ \\\\  & =⟨0,7,1⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have $x=⟨0,7,1⟩.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186269174 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "d766de83-9394-57be-84a4-bb88f5ddf792" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Magnitude of a Vector Given in Component Form"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "ef29f893-65fb-59d0-9762-8412bd3c7952" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{13}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186269176}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ef29f893-65fb-59d0-9762-8412bd3c7952" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{13}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186269176} :answer-field/id #uuid "bc8dc294-be0a-5a6e-9f56-a0b9a47b824a" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186269175} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3ef948ba-6d31-5a11-82a0-68c6d8b3b936" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186269178}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "3ef948ba-6d31-5a11-82a0-68c6d8b3b936" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186269178} :answer-field/id #uuid "4afa8a4b-12a6-51f9-ab94-d4ced4c9a18b" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186269177} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8bb13971-bdc3-56e1-8cb5-1891da11d8aa" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5\\sqrt{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186269180}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "8bb13971-bdc3-56e1-8cb5-1891da11d8aa" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5\\sqrt{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186269180} :answer-field/id #uuid "15b4644d-3a5f-5f18-aa40-3957577f54c5" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186269179}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "180fc896-0ed1-511f-b236-04a3bfb89f8b" :question/math-academy-id "q-168034" :question/problem "An ambulance service helicopter takes off from a hospital helipad three times on a particular day. The helicopter's location a few seconds after these takeoffs are given by points $P,$ $Q,$ and $R.$\n\nEarlier part 1:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13964559/assets/e589960ec2647179ac013cf60286129ece1d31e5daa8bf16fdeb237e942c92df.png)     \n                                \n                            \n\n   \n\n                            The helicopter's pilot represents the three locations in vector form, as shown in the diagram. Taking the helipad as the origin, find the coordinates of the position vectors $p,$ $q,$ and $r$ of the points $P,$ $Q,$ and $R,$ respectively.\n\n                            \n                                    \n                                        \n                                            \n\n                                                \n\n                                        \n                                        \n                                        \n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        $p=⟨$\n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                            \n                                        $0$                \n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        \n$,\\,0,\\,3⟩\\,,$ \n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                                \n\n                                                \n\n                                        \n                                        \n                                        \n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        $q=⟨0,\\,-3,\\,$\n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                            \n                                        $2$                \n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        \n$⟩\\,,$ \n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                                \n\n                                                \n\n                                        \n                                        \n                                        \n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        $r=⟨0,\\,$ \n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                            \n                                        $4$                \n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        \n$,\\,3⟩\\,.$\n\nEarlier part 2:\n\nExpress the vector $x=\\overset{\\to }{QR}$ in terms of the vectors $q$ and $r.$\n\n                            \n                                    \n                                        \n                                            \n\n                                                \n\n                                        \n                                        \n                                        \n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        $x\\,=\\,$\n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                            \n                                        $r-q$                \n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                         $\\text{ }$ (Type the vectors $q$ and $r$ as $q$ and $r$, respectively).\n\nEarlier part 3:\n\nFind the components of vector $x.$\n\n                            \n                                    \n                                        \n                                            \n\n                                                \n\n                                        \n                                        \n                                        \n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        $x=⟨$\n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                            \n                                        $0$                \n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        \n$,\\,$\n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                            \n                                        $7$                \n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        \n$,\\,$\n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                            \n                                        $1$                \n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        \n$⟩$\n\nCurrent part:\n\nFind the *exact values* of the magnitudes of vectors $q,$ $r,$ and $x.$\n\n                            \n                                    \n                                        \n                                            \n\n                                                \n\n                                        \n                                        \n                                        \n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        $|\\,q\\,|=\\,$\n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                            \n                                        {{field-1}}                \n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        \n$\\,,\\,$\n\n$|\\,r\\,|=\\,$\n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                            \n                                        {{field-2}}                \n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        \n$\\,,\\,$\n\n$|\\,x\\,|=\\,$\n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                            \n                                        {{field-3}}" :question/worked-solution "The magnitude of a vector $a$ with components $⟨{a}_{x},{a}_{y},{a}_{z}⟩$  can always be computed as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|\\,a\\,| & =\\sqrt{{a}_{x}^{2}+{a}_{y}^{2}+{a}_{z}^{2}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom part 1, we have $q=⟨0,-3,2⟩$ and $r=⟨0,4,3⟩.$ Therefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|\\,q\\,| & =\\sqrt{{0}^{2}+(-3)^{2}+{2}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{0+9+4} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{13},\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|\\,r\\,| & =\\sqrt{{0}^{2}+{4}^{2}+{3}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{0+16+9} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{25} \\\\  & =5.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom part 3, we also have $x=⟨0,7,1⟩.$ This gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|\\,x\\,| & =\\sqrt{{0}^{2}+{7}^{2}+{1}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{0+49+1} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{50} \\\\  & =5\\sqrt{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, $|\\,q\\,|=\\sqrt{13}$, $|\\,r\\,|=5$ and $|\\,x\\,|=5\\sqrt{2}.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186269181 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "68abb4f0-c532-5cb6-882c-dacfe6a945dc" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Dot Product Using the General Formula"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "04b6d5b3-6cbc-5dc3-807e-6c9f3f770958" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186269183}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "04b6d5b3-6cbc-5dc3-807e-6c9f3f770958" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186269183} :answer-field/id #uuid "783b5cc7-43dc-534a-ba87-dd7790dff1f2" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186269182}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "7ab7fa16-77ad-56db-aa2a-7cf82adf5fc6" :question/math-academy-id "q-168035" :question/problem "An ambulance service helicopter takes off from a hospital helipad three times on a particular day. The helicopter's location a few seconds after these takeoffs are given by points $P,$ $Q,$ and $R.$\n\nEarlier part 1:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13964559/assets/e589960ec2647179ac013cf60286129ece1d31e5daa8bf16fdeb237e942c92df.png)     \n                                \n                            \n\n   \n\n                            The helicopter's pilot represents the three locations in vector form, as shown in the diagram. Taking the helipad as the origin, find the coordinates of the position vectors $p,$ $q,$ and $r$ of the points $P,$ $Q,$ and $R,$ respectively.\n\n                            \n                                    \n                                        \n                                            \n\n                                                \n\n                                        \n                                        \n                                        \n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        $p=⟨$\n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                            \n                                        $0$                \n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        \n$,\\,0,\\,3⟩\\,,$ \n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                                \n\n                                                \n\n                                        \n                                        \n                                        \n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        $q=⟨0,\\,-3,\\,$\n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                            \n                                        $2$                \n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        \n$⟩\\,,$ \n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                                \n\n                                                \n\n                                        \n                                        \n                                        \n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        $r=⟨0,\\,$ \n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                            \n                                        $4$                \n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        \n$,\\,3⟩\\,.$\n\nEarlier part 2:\n\nExpress the vector $x=\\overset{\\to }{QR}$ in terms of the vectors $q$ and $r.$\n\n                            \n                                    \n                                        \n                                            \n\n                                                \n\n                                        \n                                        \n                                        \n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        $x\\,=\\,$\n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                            \n                                        $r-q$                \n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                         $\\text{ }$ (Type the vectors $q$ and $r$ as $q$ and $r$, respectively).\n\nEarlier part 3:\n\nFind the components of vector $x.$\n\n                            \n                                    \n                                        \n                                            \n\n                                                \n\n                                        \n                                        \n                                        \n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        $x=⟨$\n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                            \n                                        $0$                \n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        \n$,\\,$\n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                            \n                                        $7$                \n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        \n$,\\,$\n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                            \n                                        $1$                \n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        \n$⟩$\n\nEarlier part 4:\n\nFind the *exact values* of the magnitudes of vectors $q,$ $r,$ and $x.$\n\n                            \n                                    \n                                        \n                                            \n\n                                                \n\n                                        \n                                        \n                                        \n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        $|\\,q\\,|=\\,$\n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                            \n                                        $\\sqrt{13}$                \n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        \n$\\,,\\,$\n\n$|\\,r\\,|=\\,$\n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                            \n                                        $5$                \n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        \n$\\,,\\,$\n\n$|\\,x\\,|=\\,$\n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                            \n                                        $5\\sqrt{2}$\n\nCurrent part:\n\nFind the dot product of the vectors $q$ and $r.$\n\n                            \n                                    \n                                        \n                                            \n\n                                                \n\n                                        \n                                        \n                                        \n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        $q\\cdot r=\\,$\n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                            \n                                        {{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "The dot product of two vectors given in component form can be computed by summing up the products of corresponding components of vectors:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}q\\cdot r & ={q}_{x}\\cdot {r}_{x}+{q}_{y}\\cdot {r}_{y}+{q}_{z}\\cdot {r}_{z}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom part 1, we have $q=⟨0,-3,2⟩$ and $r=⟨0,4,3⟩.$ Therefore, the formula for the dot product gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}q\\cdot r & =0\\cdot 0+(-3)\\cdot 4+2\\cdot 3 \\\\  & =0-12+6 \\\\  & =-6.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186269184 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "a087e7bc-4e74-584d-af3b-bf6bee4b75ea" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Angle Between Two Vectors Given Their Components"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "cb4a8a57-d53e-516f-a8a4-ef13aa698402" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "109" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186269186}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "cb4a8a57-d53e-516f-a8a4-ef13aa698402" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "109" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186269186} :answer-field/id #uuid "3a0a4cb3-128e-52ff-9a2a-1aae80a37b57" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186269185}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "69699500-4554-5c7a-85c9-7002710daf2e" :question/math-academy-id "q-168036" :question/problem "An ambulance service helicopter takes off from a hospital helipad three times on a particular day. The helicopter's location a few seconds after these takeoffs are given by points $P,$ $Q,$ and $R.$\n\nEarlier part 1:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13964559/assets/e589960ec2647179ac013cf60286129ece1d31e5daa8bf16fdeb237e942c92df.png)     \n                                \n                            \n\n   \n\n                            The helicopter's pilot represents the three locations in vector form, as shown in the diagram. Taking the helipad as the origin, find the coordinates of the position vectors $p,$ $q,$ and $r$ of the points $P,$ $Q,$ and $R,$ respectively.\n\n                            \n                                    \n                                        \n                                            \n\n                                                \n\n                                        \n                                        \n                                        \n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        $p=⟨$\n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                            \n                                        $0$                \n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        \n$,\\,0,\\,3⟩\\,,$ \n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                                \n\n                                                \n\n                                        \n                                        \n                                        \n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        $q=⟨0,\\,-3,\\,$\n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                            \n                                        $2$                \n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        \n$⟩\\,,$ \n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                                \n\n                                                \n\n                                        \n                                        \n                                        \n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        $r=⟨0,\\,$ \n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                            \n                                        $4$                \n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        \n$,\\,3⟩\\,.$\n\nEarlier part 2:\n\nExpress the vector $x=\\overset{\\to }{QR}$ in terms of the vectors $q$ and $r.$\n\n                            \n                                    \n                                        \n                                            \n\n                                                \n\n                                        \n                                        \n                                        \n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        $x\\,=\\,$\n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                            \n                                        $r-q$                \n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                         $\\text{ }$ (Type the vectors $q$ and $r$ as $q$ and $r$, respectively).\n\nEarlier part 3:\n\nFind the components of vector $x.$\n\n                            \n                                    \n                                        \n                                            \n\n                                                \n\n                                        \n                                        \n                                        \n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        $x=⟨$\n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                            \n                                        $0$                \n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        \n$,\\,$\n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                            \n                                        $7$                \n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        \n$,\\,$\n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                            \n                                        $1$                \n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        \n$⟩$\n\nEarlier part 4:\n\nFind the *exact values* of the magnitudes of vectors $q,$ $r,$ and $x.$\n\n                            \n                                    \n                                        \n                                            \n\n                                                \n\n                                        \n                                        \n                                        \n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        $|\\,q\\,|=\\,$\n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                            \n                                        $\\sqrt{13}$                \n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        \n$\\,,\\,$\n\n$|\\,r\\,|=\\,$\n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                            \n                                        $5$                \n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        \n$\\,,\\,$\n\n$|\\,x\\,|=\\,$\n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                            \n                                        $5\\sqrt{2}$\n\nEarlier part 5:\n\nFind the dot product of the vectors $q$ and $r.$\n\n                            \n                                    \n                                        \n                                            \n\n                                                \n\n                                        \n                                        \n                                        \n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        $q\\cdot r=\\,$\n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                            \n                                        $-6$\n\nCurrent part:\n\nFind the angle $\\theta $ between vectors $q$ and $r.$ Round your answer to the nearest degree.\n\n                            \n                                    \n                                        \n                                            \n\n                                                \n\n                                        \n                                        \n                                        \n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        $\\theta =$\n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                            \n                                        {{field-1}}                \n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        ${}^{∘}$" :question/worked-solution "To find the angle $\\theta $ between the vectors, we can rearrange the dot product formula:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}q\\cdot r & =|\\,q\\,|\\cdot |\\,r\\,|\\cdot \\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta  \\\\ \\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta  & =\\frac{q\\cdot r}{|\\,q\\,||\\,r\\,|}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom part 4, we have $|\\,q\\,|=\\sqrt{13}$ and $|\\,r\\,|=5.$ Also, from part 5, we have $q\\cdot r=-6.$ Therefore, \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta  & =\\frac{q\\cdot r}{|\\,q\\,||\\,r\\,|} \\\\  & =\\frac{(-6)}{\\sqrt{13}\\cdot 5} \\\\  & =-\\frac{6}{5\\sqrt{13}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally,\n\n$$\n\\theta =\\operatorname{arccos}⁡(-\\frac{6}{5\\sqrt{13}})≈{109}^{∘}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186269187 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "381f7ffe-ae4b-5e45-9fa9-e2a6bd8348b3" :knowledge-point/title "Determining the Image of a Vector Under a Map Using Vector Addition and Scalar Multiplication"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "781144ec-f720-50b6-bf9e-db551e79f178" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186269189}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "781144ec-f720-50b6-bf9e-db551e79f178" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186269189} :answer-field/id #uuid "8651bd79-4a07-59b8-b3ef-7633c1ad5643" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186269188} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "087ec9c5-55c2-521d-9e3e-774f031a7ef8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186269191}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "087ec9c5-55c2-521d-9e3e-774f031a7ef8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186269191} :answer-field/id #uuid "911eb0a9-06fa-5f85-907c-af8aea84339d" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186269190} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "03b29e17-4202-5098-a20f-7dcae12f12f2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186269193}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "03b29e17-4202-5098-a20f-7dcae12f12f2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186269193} :answer-field/id #uuid "8a9f91f2-a62b-5a86-bd70-7924a1acd69e" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186269192}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "95e51b90-72e1-5d73-babc-de4eceaa6320" :question/math-academy-id "q-168037" :question/problem "An ambulance service helicopter takes off from a hospital helipad three times on a particular day. The helicopter's location a few seconds after these takeoffs are given by points $P,$ $Q,$ and $R.$\n\nEarlier part 1:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13964559/assets/e589960ec2647179ac013cf60286129ece1d31e5daa8bf16fdeb237e942c92df.png)     \n                                \n                            \n\n   \n\n                            The helicopter's pilot represents the three locations in vector form, as shown in the diagram. Taking the helipad as the origin, find the coordinates of the position vectors $p,$ $q,$ and $r$ of the points $P,$ $Q,$ and $R,$ respectively.\n\n                            \n                                    \n                                        \n                                            \n\n                                                \n\n                                        \n                                        \n                                        \n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        $p=⟨$\n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                            \n                                        $0$                \n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        \n$,\\,0,\\,3⟩\\,,$ \n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                                \n\n                                                \n\n                                        \n                                        \n                                        \n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        $q=⟨0,\\,-3,\\,$\n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                            \n                                        $2$                \n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        \n$⟩\\,,$ \n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                                \n\n                                                \n\n                                        \n                                        \n                                        \n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        $r=⟨0,\\,$ \n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                            \n                                        $4$                \n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        \n$,\\,3⟩\\,.$\n\nEarlier part 2:\n\nExpress the vector $x=\\overset{\\to }{QR}$ in terms of the vectors $q$ and $r.$\n\n                            \n                                    \n                                        \n                                            \n\n                                                \n\n                                        \n                                        \n                                        \n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        $x\\,=\\,$\n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                            \n                                        $r-q$                \n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                         $\\text{ }$ (Type the vectors $q$ and $r$ as $q$ and $r$, respectively).\n\nEarlier part 3:\n\nFind the components of vector $x.$\n\n                            \n                                    \n                                        \n                                            \n\n                                                \n\n                                        \n                                        \n                                        \n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        $x=⟨$\n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                            \n                                        $0$                \n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        \n$,\\,$\n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                            \n                                        $7$                \n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        \n$,\\,$\n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                            \n                                        $1$                \n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        \n$⟩$\n\nEarlier part 4:\n\nFind the *exact values* of the magnitudes of vectors $q,$ $r,$ and $x.$\n\n                            \n                                    \n                                        \n                                            \n\n                                                \n\n                                        \n                                        \n                                        \n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        $|\\,q\\,|=\\,$\n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                            \n                                        $\\sqrt{13}$                \n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        \n$\\,,\\,$\n\n$|\\,r\\,|=\\,$\n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                            \n                                        $5$                \n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        \n$\\,,\\,$\n\n$|\\,x\\,|=\\,$\n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                            \n                                        $5\\sqrt{2}$\n\nEarlier part 5:\n\nFind the dot product of the vectors $q$ and $r.$\n\n                            \n                                    \n                                        \n                                            \n\n                                                \n\n                                        \n                                        \n                                        \n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        $q\\cdot r=\\,$\n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                            \n                                        $-6$\n\nEarlier part 6:\n\nFind the angle $\\theta $ between vectors $q$ and $r.$ Round your answer to the nearest degree.\n\n                            \n                                    \n                                        \n                                            \n\n                                                \n\n                                        \n                                        \n                                        \n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        $\\theta =$\n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                            \n                                        $109$                \n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        ${}^{∘}$\n\nCurrent part:\n\nThe helicopter's pilot wants to consider the effect of a linear transformation $T$ such that $T(r)=⟨-8,17,3⟩$ and $T(3q+r)=⟨10,17,9⟩.$ Find the image of $q$ under the action of $T.$\n\n                            \n                                    \n                                        \n                                            \n\n                                                \n\n                                        \n                                        \n                                        \n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        $T(q)=\\,⟨$\n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                            \n                                        {{field-1}}                \n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        \n$,\\,$\n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                            \n                                        {{field-2}}                \n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        \n$,\\,$\n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                            \n                                        {{field-3}}                \n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        \n$⟩.$" :question/worked-solution "Since $T$ is a linear transformation, we have that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}T(kq+hr)=T(kq)+T(hr)=kT(q)+hT(r)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nfor any vectors $q$ and $r.$ Therefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}T(3q+r) & =3T(q)+T(r) \\\\ ⟨10,17,9⟩ & =3T(q)+⟨-8,17,3⟩ \\\\ 3T(q) & =⟨10,17,9⟩-⟨-8,17,3⟩ \\\\ 3T(q) & =⟨18,0,6⟩ \\\\ T(q) & =\\frac{1}{3}⟨18,0,6⟩ \\\\ T(q) & =⟨6,0,2⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}]}
